g advertising, 1985&#x02013;1996</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>1999</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>2055</fpage><lpage>2057</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10209012</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ferry</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Lamy</surname><given-names>PP</given-names></name><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physicians' knowledge of prescribing for the elderly. A study of primary care physicians in Pennsylvania</article-title><source>J Am Geriatr Soc</source><year>1985</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>616</fpage><lpage>625</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4031340</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bower</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Burkett</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Family physicians and generic drugs: a study of recognition, information sources, prescribing attitudes, and practices</article-title><source>J Fam Pract</source><year>1987</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>612</fpage><lpage>616</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3585265</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dajda</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Drug advertising and prescribing</article-title><source>J R Coll Gen Pract</source><year>1978</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>538</fpage><lpage>541</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">739456</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Stolley</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Lasagna</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>McEvilla</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Sloane</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Differential education concerning therapeutics and resultant physician prescribing patterns</article-title><source>J Med Educ</source><year>1972</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>118</fpage><lpage>127</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5011761</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walton</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ad Recognition and Prescribing by Physicians</article-title><source>Journal of Advertising Research</source><year>1980</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>39</fpage><lpage>48</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greving</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Denig</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Veen</surname><given-names>WJ van der</given-names></name><name><surname>Beltman</surname><given-names>FW</given-names></name><name><surname>Sturkenboom</surname><given-names>MCJM</given-names></name><name><surname>Haaijer-Ruskamp</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Determinants for the adoption of angiotensin II receptor blockers by general practitioners</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>63</volume><fpage>2890</fpage><lpage>2898</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16959390</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.socscimed.2006.07.019</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Horn</surname><given-names>FE</given-names></name><name><surname>Mandryk</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Mackson</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wutzke</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Weekes</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hyndman</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Measurement of changes in antihypertensive drug utilisation following primary care educational interventions</article-title><source>Pharmacoepidemiol Drug Saf</source><year>2007</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>297</fpage><lpage>308</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16634120</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/pds.1243</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Avorn</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hartley</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Scientific versus commercial sources of influence on the prescribing behavior of physicians</article-title><source>Am J Med</source><year>1982</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>4</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7091173</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0002-9343(82)90911-1</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Medicines Australia Inc</collab></person-group><source>Medicines Australia Code of Conduct</source><year>2003</year><edition>14</edition><publisher-name>Deakin, ACT: Medicines Australia Inc</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Australian Government Department of Health and Ageing: National Medicines Policy 2000</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.health.gov.au/internet/main/publishing.nsf/Content/nmp-objectives-policy.htm/$FILE/nmp2000.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greving</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Denig</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>de Zeeuw</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Haaijer-Ruskamp</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Claims in advertisements for antihypertensive drugs in a Dutch medical journal</article-title><source>J Hypertens</source><year>2007</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>713</fpage><lpage>722</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17278989</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/HJH.0b013e328012662a</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cardarelli</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Licciardone</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>LG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A cross-sectional evidence-based review of pharmaceutical promotional marketing brochures and their underlying studies: is what they tell us important and true?</article-title><source>BMC Fam Pract</source><year>2006</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>13</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16515686</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2296-7-13</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Loke</surname><given-names>TW</given-names></name><name><surname>Koh</surname><given-names>FC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ward</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pharmaceutical advertisement claims in Australian medical publications</article-title><source>Med J Aust</source><year>2002</year><volume>177</volume><fpage>291</fpage><lpage>293</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12225274</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilkes</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Doblin</surname><given-names>BH</given-names></name><name><surname>Shapiro</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pharmaceutical advertisements in leading medical journals: experts' assessments</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>1992</year><volume>116</volume><fpage>912</fpage><lpage>919</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1580449</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lankinen</surname><given-names>KS</given-names></name><name><surname>Levola</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Marttinen</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Puumalainen</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Helin-Salmivaara</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Industry guidelines, laws and regulations ignored: quality of drug advertising in medical journals</article-title><source>Pharmacoepidemiol Drug Saf</source><year>2004</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>789</fpage><lpage>795</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15486957</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/pds.1017</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>European Society of Hypertension-European Society of Cardiology Guidelines Committee</collab></person-group><article-title>2003 European Society of Hypertension-European Society of Cardiology guidelines for the management of arterial hypertension</article-title><source>J Hypertens</source><year>2003</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>1011</fpage><lpage>1053</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12777938</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00004872-200306000-00001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="book"><source>Australian Medicines Handbook</source><year>2003</year><edition>4</edition><publisher-name>Ad